registers the data series only using data whithin the mask.\n\n\
RegisterData[target, {moving, mask, vox}] registers the data series using the \
given voxel size only using data within the mask.\nRegisterData[{target, \
mask}, {moving, mask, vox}] registers the data series using the given voxel \
size only using data within the mask.\nRegisterData[{target, vox}, {moving, \
mask, vox}] registers the data series using the given voxel size only using \
data within the mask.\nRegisterData[{target, mask, vox}, moving] registers \
the data series using the given voxel size only using data within the mask.\n\
RegisterData[{target, mask, vox}, {moving, mask}] registers the data series \
using the given voxel size only using data within the mask.\n\
RegisterData[{target, mask, vox}, {moving, vox}] registers the data series \
using the given voxel size only using data within the mask.\n\
RegisterData[{target, mask}, {moving, vox}] registers the data series using \
the given voxel size only using data within the mask.\nRegisterData[{target, \
vox}, {moving, mask}] registers the data series using the given voxel size \
only using data within the mask.\n\nOutput is the registered data with the \
dimensions of the moving data. \nIf OutputTransformation is True it also \
outputs the translation, rotation scale and skew of all images or volumes.\n\n\
RegisterData[] is based on DOI: 10.1109/TMI.2009.2035616 and \
10.3389/fninf.2013.00050.", 
