correction of the spectra by minimizing the difference between the real and \
absolute spectra velaue.\\nPhaseCorrectSpectra[spec, dw] performs 0th order \
phase correction of the spectra using Henkel matrix SVD \
fitting.\\nPhaseCorrectSpectra[spec, dw, te] := performs 0th and 1st order \
phase correction of the spectra using Henkel matrix SVD fitting. The first \
order phase is corrected by padding the fid with the missing values in the \
time befroe the TE.\\nPhaseCorrectSpectra[spec, dw, te, gyro, ppmRan] \
performs 0th and 1st order phase correction of the spectra using Henkel \
matrix SVD fitting. Only the part of the spectra in the ppmRan is used for \
optimization.\"\>", "InformationUsageText",
